.TH BYTE_RSKIPN 3
.SH NAME
byte_rskipn \- count the run of bytes other than a given byte at the end of a byte array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t byte_rskipn(const void* " p ", size_t " n ", char " c ");
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_rskipn
returns the number of consecutive bytes not equal to c at the end of p.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The run length; if c does not occur at all, it returns n; if n is 0, it returns 0.
.PP
These are the single-byte counterparts of the scan_charset*skip functions.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_skipn (3),
.BR byte_rskip (3),
.BR byte_rchr (3)
